6. Types of Web Pages
There are two types of webpages:
Static Webpage
Dynamic Webpage
6.1 Static Webpage
Content remains the same.
User interaction (UI) is comparatively less.
Less usage of database interaction.
Content is displayed similarly to all users.
Example: Wikipedia (basic static content pages).
Dynamic Webpage
Content differs for each individual based on their preferences.
User interaction is more.
Content can reflect the user's activities and requirements.
Database management is necessary.
Examples:
Instagram Reels
Chats
Personalized social media feeds.
